A||N||6||FieroSTETZ||ignition coil?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||12-14-2000||11:19 PM||||a while back i changed my ignition coil due to the symptoms as follows: the car would occasionally stumble while driving in a straight line, at constant speed or accelerating, and when sitting in place, it would randomly die. i replaced the ignition coil and the problem went away for about 3 months, and now it has started up again. today it started doing it again, and with the car running, if i wiggle the coil around, it stumbles and dies. i suspect either another dead coil, or maybe the 13 year old wiring going to it. my car shouldnt be eating an msd blaster ignition coil every 3 months- how do i test either the coil, or the wiring around it? this is currently my only form of transportation. is there any way i can buy a whole new wiring harness somewhere? (not for now, but soon the car goes under the knife for a 3.4 and a 4puck kevlar clutch) thanks for any help- gotta get it working by 8 am saturday, or no work for me!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tom88gt||12-14-2000||11:55 PM||||Use an ohm meter to test the coil.  Haynes will tell you how.  You might want to take a close look at all your connections.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||12-15-2000||01:01 AM||||could this happen if the coil has been getting overheated? is it safe to relocate the coil to the firewall or something?||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||12-15-2000||01:16 AM||||FieroSTETZ, you might want to change your ignition module rather than the coil this time - we had a car here in the shop with the same symptoms as you described and that was the problem. Does the "Check Engine" light come on? If so, do you know what code is being sent? Also, you might want to check the connections to the ignition module, and the IAC as well...........<P>Who is doing your 3.4 upgrade with the Kevlar clutch?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||12-15-2000||01:57 AM||||mostly me, with my dad helping. he and i put the smallblock in our bug, and turbocharged his old 914... this shouldn't be too complicated, its not a major swap or anyhting, just redrilling some holes. now the v8 in the beetle... that things not a bug anymore||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||12-15-2000||01:58 AM||||the only code i ever get is a code 32... how much is an ignition module, and how hard to change? also, how much would a shop charge for a 3.4 swap and new clutch, parts and labor? (i worke about 55-60 hours a week, not a lot of time to work||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-15-2000||08:10 AM||||You can move your coil anywhere wires will reach. make sure its got a good clean ground. spray WD40 in connectors to clean them. any loose or corroded connectors can cause a failure. Module only cost $25-$30. to replace just take off dist cap, screw and unplug the old one. BTW could be a bad pickup coil inside the distributor too. only cost $15, but you have to remove dist to replace it.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-15-2000).]||||reg||1
